{"id":"6c40656b77cd","path":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/career-prospects","lang":"en","title":"Employability","description":"Great career prospects ahead! Discover what happens after the Master in European Studies in Investor Relations and Financial Communication and the opportunies that are waiting for you.","section":"Education","crumbs":["Education","Master","ESIR","Career Prospects"],"image":null,"words":125,"alternates":{"en":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/career-prospects"},"breadcrumb":[{"label":"Home","path":"/en"},{"label":"Education","path":"/en/originalnode/8525"},{"label":"Master","path":"/en/originalnode/7757"},{"label":"ESIR","path":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication"},{"label":"Career Prospects","path":null},{"label":"Employability","path":null}],"blocks":[{"t":"html","html":"<p>A Master in European Studies in Investor Relations and Financial Communication has become a significant asset and can open many doors for graduates looking to kick-start their careers in financial communication.</p> <p>The overall employment rate* of the programme is 100%. Over one-third of the graduates (35%) accept a job in Switzerland, 58% in Italy, and the remaining 4% around the globe. Most graduates (59.5%) find an occupation in the finance sector. </p> <table> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>Main sectors</strong></td> <td><strong>%</strong></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Finance</td> <td>59.5</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Consulting</td> <td>15.0</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Energy</td> <td>7.5</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Public Administration</td> <td>7.5</td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> </td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Main functions</strong></td> <td><strong>%</strong></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Finance</td> <td>65.0</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Communication &amp; PR</td> <td>30.0</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Marketing</td> <td>5.0</td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> </td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Place of work</strong></td> <td><strong>%</strong></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Switzerland <ul> <li>Ticino</li> <li>Other Swiss Cantons</li> </ul> </td> <td>35.0 <ul> <li>16.0</li> <li>19.0</li> </ul> </td> </tr> <tr> <td>Italy</td> <td>58.0</td> </tr> <tr> <td>World (other Countries)</td> <td>4.0</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><em>*The statistics are based on the first two classes of ESIR graduates (2022-2023).</em></p>"}],"ctas":[{"label":"Apply Now","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/application"},{"label":"Learn More","href":"mailto:esir@usi.ch"}],"nav":[{"label":"Master in European Studies in Investor Relations and Financial Communication","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication"},{"label":"Study plan","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/structure-and-contents"},{"label":"Employability","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/career-prospects"},{"label":"Job Profiles","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/career-prospects/job-profiles"},{"label":"Employers","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/career-prospects/employers"},{"label":"Career Stories","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/career-prospects/career-stories"},{"label":"Application and admission","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/admission"},{"label":"Fees and Grants","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/fees-and-grants"},{"label":"Practical Information","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/organising-your-studies"},{"label":"Open days and study advisory","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/open-days-study-advisory"},{"label":"FAQ","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-financial-communication/faq"},{"label":"Contact us","href":"/en/education/master/investor-relations-fina